{
  "name": "Request Google Reviews on WhatsApp and Draft AI Replies in the Reviewer's Language",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Review + Auto-Reply (Clinic Reputation)\n\n**Part 1 — Review Request:** A daily Schedule Trigger reads the *Completed Visits* Google Sheet, filters visits not yet asked, sends each patient a WhatsApp message containing the clinic's Google review link, then marks the row as requested.\n\n**Part 2 — Review Auto-Reply:** A daily Schedule Trigger reads new rows from the *Reviews* sheet (reviewer_name, rating, review_text). An AI Agent (OpenAI gpt-4o-mini) drafts a warm, professional reply — thanks happy reviewers, apologizes + offers to make it right for unhappy ones without admitting fault — and writes it back to the sheet. If rating ≤ 3, the manager gets a Telegram alert.\n\n**Tools/APIs:** Google Sheets OAuth2 · WhatsApp Business Cloud · OpenAI · Telegram.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Google Business Profile API (OAuth + business verification) is required to auto-FETCH and auto-POST Google reviews live; that verification is a real hurdle, so this workflow uses a Google Sheet as the review source/destination so it works TODAY, and the GBP API can be wired in later to replace the sheet.**\n\n**TODO before running:** set both Google Sheet documentIds, confirm sheet + column names, replace the placeholder review link, and confirm WhatsApp / Telegram / OpenAI credentials.\n\n---\n**Author:** Jitendra Kavire ([n8nebooks.com](https://n8nebooks.com)). Full node-by-node setup guide: https://n8nebooks.com/ebook/n8n-clinic-hospital-automations/chapter/4",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 1680,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "bf2ce576-0d18-405f-b635-99754cc3017b",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
